      "title": "[agro-tv.ro] Romania vaccinates sheep and goats to restore live exports",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://agro-tv.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ovine-1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nRomania began free emergency vaccination of sheep and goats on Oct. 25 in Constanta and Tulcea, aiming to immunize about 800,000 animals in the two southeastern counties. The campaign targets sheep and goat pox and, in the two counties, peste des petits ruminants; authorities say disease controls are needed before live-animal exports to non-EU markets can resume.\n\nThe country received 1.1 million vaccine doses from European Union reserves. Vaccination and veterinary services are free to farmers. Temporary restrictions on sheep and goat movements remain in force nationwide, and the veterinary authority has not set a date for resuming live exports.",
