      "id": "http://www.dagenslantbruk.se/lantbrukets-kostnadskris-la-mnas-ola-st",
      "url": "http://www.dagenslantbruk.se/lantbrukets-kostnadskris-la-mnas-ola-st",
      "title": "[dagenslantbruk.se] Swedish farmers’ federation says spring budget leaves input-cost crisis unresolved",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.dagenslantbruk.se/upload/article/bild/8773/1088995/LRF-Dagenslantbruk.se_s.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nThe Federation of Swedish Farmers (LRF) said Sweden’s spring budget failed to ease high farm costs, especially for diesel and fertilizer, even as policymakers call for increased domestic food production. Farmer representatives on Arla’s board said cheaper groceries do not necessarily mean lower production costs.\n\nLRF president Palle Borgström said higher costs could force some farm businesses to stop production and urged the government to prevent EU climate tariffs from making fertilizer more expensive. The budget increased funding for food and water preparedness and nitrogen-efficiency investments, but LRF said it did not address farmers’ most urgent economic pressures.",
